	"WHAT IS NEW?": "HDI2_Title1",
	"Text areas and input objects can now use padding and vertical alignment. These properties give you precise control over the space around text and where text sits inside its area.": "HDI2_Desc1",
	"WHAT DOES THIS FEATURE BRING?": "HDI2_Title2",
	"Set independent padding values for each side of a text area or input, then align the text at the top, center, or bottom. This makes multi-line fields clearer and helps form layouts match their intended design.": "HDI2_Desc2",
	"WHAT TO EXPECT IN THIS HDI?": "HDI2_Title3",
	"The following tabs show how padding and vertical alignment affect text areas and input objects, and provide examples you can play with to better visualize what's possible.": "HDI2_Desc3",
	"4 WAYS TO SET PADDING & ALIGNMENT": "HDI2_PageTitle2",
	"Set the padding and verticalAlign properties directly in the form's JSON source, using \"paddingLeft\", \"paddingRight\", \"paddingTop\", \"paddingBottom\", and \"verticalAlign\" keys.": "HDI2_JsonDesc",
	"Apply padding and vertical-align through either 4D specific or standard CSS keys; that way, you can style your form the same way you would style a web page.": "HDI2_CssDesc",
	"PROPERTY LIST": "HDI2_PropListTitle",
	"Use the Property List in the Form editor to set Padding and Vertical Alignment visually, without writing any code.": "HDI2_PropListDesc",
	"COMMANDS": "HDI2_CommandsTitle",
	"Change padding and alignment at runtime with the  OBJECT SET VERTICAL ALIGNMENT command, and the new OBJECT SET PADDING command.": "HDI2_CommandsDesc",
	"PADDING & VERTICAL ALIGNMENT": "HDI2_PageTitle3",
	"TEXT AREA": "HDI2_PaddingTitle",
	"With padding and vertical alignment, you can now precisely position text within text area objects and adjust the spacing on all four sides.": "HDI2_PaddingDesc",
	"This text shows how padding and vertical alignment position it inside the text area.": "HDI2_StaticTextSample",
	"INPUT": "HDI2_AlignTitle",
	"Input objects also support padding and vertical alignment, useful for spacing text from the borders or making room for icons like the ones shown here.": "HDI2_AlignDesc",
